{"skill":{"slug":"rss-reader","displayName":"RSS Reader"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771723745290,"changelog":"Initial release: Monitor RSS/Atom feeds for content research","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3638,"sha256":"8dc837e1c639b304a2e9ed5db48aca29011305c768718292a76015534719dd69","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"data/feeds.json","size":596,"sha256":"e255cca63f4e78608506183d862c055d1fceff76ef658be438343dd774c2d5ad","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/rss.js","size":11208,"sha256":"c2e8c62122cf63cfa66659c258f834a703eb7724aba154c2af92feb4661cb298","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2436,"sha256":"ccfd5830646034662fdbc659641bcfdea0c0c98f3981e1a9cf20bc615c90d9cb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789077834688,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f498c7eebaff8b5057227a2d7cfa828761cdaa179aa566a557aacae68596f101","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f498c7eebaff8b5057227a2d7cfa828761cdaa179aa566a557aacae68596f101","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: rss-reader\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is suspicious due to a significant prompt injection vulnerability. The `SKILL.md` explicitly instructs the AI agent to 'summarize new items worth reading' from RSS feeds, especially when using the `--format ideas` option. The `scripts/rss.js` script fetches content from user-controlled URLs and directly embeds the `item.title` and `item.description` (after basic HTML entity decoding) into the markdown output that the agent is instructed to summarize. This allows an attacker who controls an RSS feed to inject malicious instructions into the agent's prompt, potentially leading to unauthorized actions. While the script itself doesn't contain malicious code, this interaction creates a critical attack surface.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166092238},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":58,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":15,"checkedAt":1789077834688},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This RSS reader mostly matches its stated purpose, but it fetches arbitrary feed URLs from the host environment without internal-network safeguards and prints remote feed text unsanitized.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Feed fetching accepts arbitrary URLs and follows redirects without restricting loopback, private, link-local, or metadata endpoints, which is broader host-network access than an RSS reader needs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install hook or hidden installer was found; documentation mentions npm dependencies and a parser module that are not actually present or needed by the inspected script.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The description is broad and could trigger for many research/news tasks; commands are user-directed, but safer activation boundaries and warnings would improve clarity.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The script stores feed configuration and check timestamps in artifact/data/feeds.json and suggests optional cron/heartbeat scheduling, but no automatic persistence or privilege escalation was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill is coherently an RSS/Atom feed manager for adding, checking, listing, filtering, and summarizing feeds.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the feed URLs you will add and the environment does not expose sensitive localhost, private-network, or cloud metadata services to this process. Prefer adding URL validation, redirect limits, private-address blocking, response-size limits, and terminal-output sanitization before broad use or scheduled checks.","findings":"[AE1] expected: The referenced script is present in this workspace and was fully inspected, so the partial-inspection concern is downgraded to scanner coverage noise rather than artifact behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad RSS/news monitoring language fits the skill purpose, though narrower trigger guidance would reduce unintended activation.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persisting feed URLs and contacting remote feed servers are expected for an RSS reader, but the skill should disclose the local storage path and outbound network behavior more clearly.\n[T09] unexpected: The SSRF concern is artifact-supported: scripts/rss.js fetches user-supplied and stored URLs, follows redirects recursively, and does not block local or private network targets.\n[T09] unexpected: The terminal control-sequence concern is artifact-supported: remote feed titles, descriptions, names, categories, and links are printed without sanitizing control characters.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789077834688}}}}}